@DarkLight1337 sorry for the slow reply. Part of the reasoning above has changed but I still think there's a case for the chat path. With #63103 merged, `output_mode: "derender"` streams parsed output from generate which means the caller doesn't carry stream state or need a separate derender frontend. It does need the tokenizer and parsers on the generate server. What generate doesn't return is OpenAI chat chunks, so the router has to rebuild them.[ llm-d-router#3656](https://github.com/llm-d/llm-d-router/issues/3656) went with forwarded IDs on the client's route as its default which keeps the native response.

The bigger concern for me is that I don't see a gate. This accepts client supplied tensors on `/v1/chat/completions` with no KV connector or `--enable-scale-out` check which means it's open on a plain `vllm serve`. The blue/red test in the description shows the model answering from something other than `messages` which is #62307 with images. I think this should follow whatever we decide on #62333.

@praveingk one question on payload. Forwarded tensors are about 8 KB per image token unless they hit the cache and the original image stays in `messages`. [ llm-d-router#3656](https://github.com/llm-d/llm-d-router/issues/3656) lists no rendered tensors across the gateway in its acceptance and [llm-d-router#3706](https://github.com/llm-d/llm-d-router/pull/3706) needs `vllm.omitMMKwargs: false` to send them. How do you see those fitting together?

